# @see R-030 (Design Patterns vs Native Platform Features)
id: PATTERN-001
ilities: [analysability]
source: cpm
maturity: 3
action: advisory
title: Singleton getInstance() in module-based language
category: quality
severity: warning
engine: pattern
target:
  extensions: .ts .js .tsx .jsx .py .rb .go .kt .php
  exclude_paths: test/ tests/ vendor/ node_modules/ .git/ build/ dist/
patterns:
  - regex: static\s+getInstance\s*\(
    message: "Manual Singleton pattern — in module-based languages, module scope is already a singleton. Use module exports or framework DI (@Injectable, @Service) instead"
  - regex: private\s+static\s+\w*[Ii]nstance
    message: "Singleton instance field — module-scope variables are singletons by design in TS/JS/Python/Go/Ruby"
  - regex: private\s+constructor\s*\(\s*\)
    message: "Private constructor for Singleton — consider module-scope or DI-managed singleton instead"
fix: Remove getInstance() pattern. In TypeScript/JavaScript, export a module-level instance. In Python, use module-level variables. In frameworks (Angular, NestJS, Spring), use @Injectable()/@Service() — DI manages lifecycle.
